        "title": "Carbonates and Phosphates",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nCALCITE: CaCO₃ (trigonal, R3̄c)\n  Most abundant carbonate; forms at Earth surface conditions\n  Hardness: 3 (scratched by a penny; scratches fingernail)\n  Perfect rhombohedral cleavage: {1011} — three planes at ~75°\n  Effervesces vigorously in cold dilute HCl (definitive field test)\n  Strongly birefringent: \"double refraction\" — two images through crystal\n  Isotropy: Iceland spar (optical calcite) used in Nicol prisms"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-CARBONATES-PHOSPHATES.md#007",
      "path": [
        "05-CARBONATES-PHOSPHATES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:mineralogy:05-carbonates-phosphates, git-history:mineralogy:05-carbonates-phosphates]",
