        "root_concepts": "[carbonates, phosphates]",
        "section": "mineralogy",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Carbonates and Phosphates",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "FORMS OF CALCITE:\n  Marble: metamorphosed limestone; coarser crystal mosaic\n  Travertine: hot-spring deposited; layered, often tan/orange\n  Tufa: cold-spring deposited; porous; towers in saline lakes\n  Cave speleothems: stalactites, stalagmites, flowstones, cave pearls\n  Chalk: soft, porous marine limestone; coccolithophore shells\n  Bioclastic limestone: fragments of shells, corals, foraminifera\n  Oolite: concentric layers around grain nuclei; shallow-marine carbonate"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-CARBONATES-PHOSPHATES.md#008",
      "path": [
        "05-CARBONATES-PHOSPHATES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
