        "section": "mineralogy",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Carbonates and Phosphates",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "CALCITE POLYMORPHS:\n  Calcite (trigonal): stable at low T/P (Earth surface)\n  Aragonite (orthorhombic): stable at higher P; in subducting slabs\n  Vaterite: metastable hexagonal polymorph; rare; in some biominerals\n  → All have formula CaCO₃; different crystal structures\n```"
    },
