      "text": "```\nARAGONITE: CaCO₃ (orthorhombic)\n  Formed at higher P than calcite; in deep-sea sediments, high-P veins\n  Also in some mollusc shells (nacre/mother of pearl is aragonite)\n  Metastable at Earth surface → slowly converts to calcite\n  Ancient shell fossils: aragonite → calcite conversion over time\n    → Loss of original isotope/trace element chemistry"
    },
