      "text": "## The Carbonate System and Carbon Cycle"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-CARBONATES-PHOSPHATES.md#023",
      "path": [
        "05-CARBONATES-PHOSPHATES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:mineralogy:05-carbonates-phosphates, git-history:mineralogy:05-carbonates-phosphates]",
        "canonical_path": "mineralogy/05-CARBONATES-PHOSPHATES.md",
        "concepts": "[carbonates, phosphates]",
        "current_path": "mineralogy/05-CARBONATES-PHOSPHATES.md",
        "id": "maxim:mineralogy:carbonates-phosphates",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "mineralogy",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[carbonates, phosphates]",
        "section": "mineralogy",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Carbonates and Phosphates",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nEARTH'S CARBON RESERVOIRS (approximate, in Gt C)\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|  Marine carbonates (CaCO₃)          60,000,000  ← dominant       |\n|  Kerogen + coal (sedimentary organic)  15,000,000                |\n|  Mantle                              ~100,000,000 (poorly known) |\n|  Terrestrial biomass                      550                    |\n|  Soil carbon                            1,500                    |\n|  Ocean (dissolved)                      38,000                   |\n|  Atmosphere (CO₂)                          800  ← small!         |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-CARBONATES-PHOSPHATES.md#024",
      "path": [
        "05-CARBONATES-PHOSPHATES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:mineralogy:05-carbonates-phosphates, git-history:mineralogy:05-carbonates-phosphates]",
