      "text": "**Speleothem paleoclimate records**: Oxygen isotope ratios (δ¹⁸O) in speleothem calcite record past rainfall amount and source, with a temperature component. Uranium-thorium (U-Th) dating gives precise ages independent of the climate signal — unlike ice cores (layer counting) or ocean sediment cores (orbital tuning). Together they produce high-resolution climate records extending back 500,000+ years, and some Chinese cave records reach 640,000 years."
    }
